The loop now walks raw pointers from `data()` to `data() + size()`. This drops the per-iteration `size()` reload and the signed-int cast. Each element is still compared with `GetNum() == fieldNum`, and the first match returns true, so results and side effects are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Mesg::HasField(const int fieldNum) const
{
    const Field* p = fields.data();
    const Field* const end = p + fields.size();
    for (; p != end; ++p)
    {
        if (p->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return FIT_TRUE;
    }

    return FIT_FALSE;
}
```